    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player or team to move all 4 marbles from the Holding Pen around the board and into your Home Base (center area).',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Turn Sequence**: On your turn, play one card from your hand to move a marble. Draw one card from your deck to return to 5-card hand (unless the card says 'Play Again'). 2. **Exiting the Pen**: You can only move a marble OUT of the Holding Pen with specific 'Start' cards (Joker, Ace, King, Queen, Jack, or 6). These cards can also move your marble forward that many spaces. 3. **Forward Movement**: Play a card matching its number value. Face cards (K, Q, J) can move 10 spaces or exit the Pen. 4. **Backwards Movement (4s)**: The 4 is unique: play a 4 to move a marble BACKWARD 4 spaces. This is a powerful defensive move. 5. **Split Movement (7s)**: Play a 7 to move a single marble 7 spaces OR split the 7 between two different marbles (e.g., 3+4 or 2+5). 6. **Joker (Trump Card)**: Move a marble to any opponent's exact position (bumping them back to their Holding Pen) OR use as a Start card. Play Again. 7. **Play Again Cards**: Aces, 6s, Face Cards, and Jokers grant an extra turn (draw card, take another turn). 8. **Landing on Fast Track**: If you land exactly on a Fast Track entry space, you may use the central shortcut on your next turn to jump across the board.",
      'Scoring example: Winner determined by first player/team to place all 4 marbles in Home Base. First player or team to move all 4 marbles from Holding Pen, around the track, and into Home Base..',
